  "pink": "Changes relative to 2026 FIA F1 Regulations - Section F [Operational] – Iss 06, approved by the WMSC on 28/04/26",
  "red": "a. The ﬁrst period of fourteen (14) consecutive calendar days during the months of July and/or August. If two consecutive Events during this period are separated by only seventeen (17) days a shutdown period of thirteen (13) consecutive calendar days must be observed. b. The second period, only from 2023, of nine (9) consecutive calendar days starting on the 24 December. Power Units for the 2022-2025 Championships must be concurrent between the two Power Unit programmes (2022-2025, and 2026-2030). and/or unions impose a diaerent closing week, these factories may replace one week out of two weeks of the shutdown period speciﬁed in Article F3.1.1a. by the locally imposed week and have their second shutdown period speciﬁed in Article F3.1.1b. starting no later than 31 December. PU Manufacturers aaected by this must make a declaration to the FIA that the staa concerned will not be permitted to transfer to work in the country that isn’t shutdown during these periods. thirty (30) days of the start of the Championship of that year. instruct a third-party supplier to carry out any of the following activities for or on behalf of the PU Manufacturer: a. Any work activity by any employee, consultant or sub-contractor engaged in design, development or production (excluding any work activity to be undertaken at the circuit in preparation for the Event immediately following the shutdown periods).",
